<p>“The fool doth think he is wise, but the wise man knows himself to be a fool”</p>
<p><img src="https://your-website-url.example.com/posts/welcome/thumbnail.jpg" class="img-fluid"></p>
<p>Shenanigans aside, this should serve to elucidate the purpose of this website. Perhaps, in a sense, the world was too boring. And I, being a member of said world, am also boring.</p>
<div class="quarto-figure quarto-figure-center">
<figure class="figure">
<p><img src="https://your-website-url.example.com/posts/welcome/image.jpg" class="img-fluid quarto-figure quarto-figure-center figure-img"></p>
</figure>
</div>
<p>I get bored. Too bored. I need things to occupy my time. I also need a way of “focusing” my projects. It would seem my mind is a zero, containing all things — but mostly no things at all!</p>
<p>Aye, that reminds me. Some time ago when I was pondering. Everything? Nothing? Who knows. Suddenly, a stroke of genius hit me! Yet, I was so lost in (no) thought that I did not even here. Until said thought began screaming — O so loud! And I turned to myself and said “Etc, etc, etc” or however it went. The point being is that I would like to document stray thoughts. They escape me otherwise.</p>
<p>Also, I would like to more fully develop those “stray thoughts” into “stray projects”(?) But, I am thinking to make this more of an informal explanation of tips and tricks that I have come across.</p>
<p>Ah! To resist the urge to demonstrate… Should I? A little example would not hurt. No, it would not hurt at all.</p>
